[2026-10-07 06:08:27] [generation-agent.stderr] {"at":"2026-10-07T06:08:27.820Z","type":"probe_reviewed","packetId":"packet-req-1-4","detail":{"verdict":"corrected","rationale":"The failed case reloaded the revoked default browser while it was still on the public home page, then expected the sign-in label. The scenario requires reloading the revoked browser on a protected page so revocation forces return to sign-in and blocks the protected workspace. The observed home page with zero match for “Username or email” does not disprove that protected-page denial; the plan must first put the revoked browser on “Active sessions” before the other browser revokes it. Only that failure case is affected and is rebuilt with the protected-page navigation in its suffix; other cases remain unchanged.","beforePlanSha256":"64f8e21dda16aa0f5e436cf4db252542c08f578bf7835cecceac5327c6a1dac4","planSha256":"65a92a656e1db86d0e7d00872d38cfdb27b4f1decbb107f3aa410ba81e2a2a7c","corrections":[{"caseId":"req-1-4-revoked-browser-denied","conflict":"The plan reloads the revoked default browser while it is still on the public home page and expects the sign-in form. The requirement and scenario require the revoked browser to return to sign-in and be denied the protected workspace; reloading a public home page does not establish the protected-page redirect, so the observed home page is a preparation gap rather than proof of the expected denial.","basis":["The revoked browser is redirected to the sign-in page","cannot access the protected workspace, while the other browser still displays `evo-session-owner-s3`.","The system pre-provisions `evo-session-owner-s3` and two active browser sessions using the verified credentials `evo.session.owner.s3@evolution.test` and `Evo-Password-987!`."]}]},"runId":"eec581de-1871-433f-95b6-746ad72d8cff","eventId":"eec581de-1871-433f-95b6-746ad72d8cff:84","sequence":84,"phase":"probe","elapsedMs":1486543,"acceptedSha":"9cf2a0db974f87747aae629e2f5aa818d696080e","attempt":